  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#processing-model\n\nPer the HTML standard the processing model for image maps looks at the node document. That seems wrong and would bypass shadow tree boundaries.\n\nI propose that we introduce a new first step that looks at the `img` or `object` element's root and verifies that is a document. And if true uses that as the context node for parsing the hash-name reference.\n\nIf we want to make this work in shadow trees, I suggest we first verify that the element's \"shadow-host-including root\" (term to be introduced someplace) is a document and then use the element's root (which will be either a document or a ShadowRoot object at that point) as a context node for finding the `map`.\n\nLet me know what you think.\n\nPaging @hayatoito @smaug---- @rniwa.\n",
